# Deriving ADSL from SDTM

ADSL is a one-record-per-subject analysis dataset. Below is the derivation for each requested variable, with the source, logic, and SAS-style code.

---

## Setup — pull the three sources

```sas
/* 1. DM: subject-level base (one record per USUBJID) */
proc sort data=sdtm.dm out=adsl; by usubjid; run;

/* 2. EX: collapse exposure to one row per subject (first/last dose) */
proc sort data=sdtm.ex; by usubjid exstdtc; run;

data ex_first;
  set sdtm.ex;
  by usubjid;
  if first.usubjid then do; trtsdt = input(exstdtc, yymmdd10.); output; end;  /* first dose start */
run;

data ex_last;
  set sdtm.ex;
  by usubjid exendtc;
  if last.usubjid then do; trtedt = input(exendtc, yymmdd10.); output; end;   /* last dose end   */
run;

/* 3. DS: subject disposition (randomized, completed, etc.) */
proc sort data=sdtm.ds; by usubjid; run;
```

---

## 1. SAFFL — Safety Flag (received dose)

**Source:** EX (any dosing record) — optionally corroborated by DS.
**Logic:** `"Y"` if the subject has ≥1 record in EX (received study drug), else `" "`.

```sas
proc sql;
  create table ex_flag as
  select distinct usubjid, "Y" as saffl
  from sdtm.ex
  where exdose > 0;        /* or simply: any EX record present */
quit;

data adsl;
  merge adsl(in=a) ex_flag(in=b);
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  if not b then saffl = " ";   /* not dosed → blank */
run;
```

> Note: SAFFL is sometimes defined as "received any dose per the protocol-specific safety definition" and may reference DS (e.g., `DSDECOD = "ONGOING"`/`"COMPLETED"`). The EX-based rule is the standard default.

---

## 2. ITTFL — Intent-To-Treat Flag (randomized)

**Source:** DM.ARM / DM.ARMCD (and/or DS with `DSDECOD = "RANDOMIZED"`).
**Logic:** `"Y"` if the subject was randomized (assigned a treatment arm), else `" "`.

```sas
data adsl;
  set adsl;
  if arm ne "SCREEN FAILURE" and armcd not in ("","SCRNFAIL","NOTASSGN","NOT TREATED")
     then ittfl = "Y";
  else ittfl = " ";
run;
```

> Alternative: derive from DS where `DSDECOD = "RANDOMIZED"`. DM-based and DS-based should agree; prefer DM.ARMCD per the study's SAP.

---

## 3. TRT01P / TRT01A — Planned & Actual Treatment

- **TRT01P** (Planned Treatment, Period 01): from **DM.ARM**.
- **TRT01A** (Actual Treatment, Period 01): from **EX** — the treatment actually received; if not dosed, set to `"NOT TREATED"` (or keep `"NOT TREATED"` per SAP convention).

```sas
data adsl;
  set adsl;
  length trt01p trt01a $40;
  trt01p = arm;                         /* planned from DM */

  if saffl = "Y" then trt01a = arm;     /* dosed → actual = planned treatment taken */
  else                trt01a = "NOT TREATED";
run;
```

> If EX carries a treatment identifier (`EXTRT`), map `TRT01A` from the dosed value rather than DM.ARM:
> `select max(extrt) into :trt from sdtm.ex where usubjid=...`

---

## 4. TRTSDT / TRTEDT — Treatment Start & End Dates

- **TRTSDT:** earliest `EX.EXSTDTC`.
- **TRTEDT:** latest `EX.EXENDTC`.

```sas
proc sql;
  create table ex_dates as
  select usubjid,
         min(input(exstdtc,yymmdd10.)) as trtsdt format=yymmdd10.,
         max(input(exendtc,yymmdd10.)) as trtedt format=yymmdd10.
  from sdtm.ex
  group by usubjid;
quit;

data adsl;
  merge adsl ex_dates;
  by usubjid;
  format trtsdt trtedt yymmdd10.;
run;
```

---

## Final ADSL structure

```sas
data adam.adsl(keep=usubjid age sex arm trt01p trt01a
                       trtsdt trtedt saffl ittfl);
  set adsl;
  label
    saffl  = "Safety Population Flag"
    ittfl  = "Intent-To-Treat Population Flag"
    trt01p = "Planned Treatment for Period 01"
    trt01a = "Actual Treatment for Period 01"
    trtsdt = "Date of First Exposure to Treatment"
    trtedt = "Date of Last Exposure to Treatment";
run;
```

---

## Summary of source → target mapping

| ADSL Var | Source | Rule |
|----------|--------|------|
| **SAFFL** | EX | `"Y"` if ≥1 dose in EX |
| **ITTFL** | DM.ARM / DS | `"Y"` if randomized (arm assigned) |
| **TRT01P** | DM.ARM | Planned treatment |
| **TRT01A** | EX (or DM.ARM if dosed) | Actual treatment; `"NOT TREATED"` if not dosed |
| **TRTSDT** | EX.EXSTDTC | `min()` dosing start date |
| **TRTEDT** | EX.EXENDTC | `max()` dosing end date |

**Key caveats:**
- Exact flag definitions should match the **Statistical Analysis Plan (SAP)**; population rules vary by study.
- Date format/derivation (`EXSTDTC`/`EXENDTC` are ISO-8601 partial dates in SDTM) — handle partial dates (e.g., month/year only) with study-specific imputation.
- `ARMCD`/`ARM` in DM should reflect the randomized assignment; use `--CD`/`--DECOD` codes consistently between TRT01P/TRT01A and any TRTn variables.

# Deriving ADSL from SDTM (DM, EX, DS)

Below is the standard ADaM derivation logic plus production SAS code for each requested variable. ADSL is a one-record-per-subject (`USUBJID`) analysis dataset built from the SDTM `SUPPQUAL`-aware domains.

---

## Step 0 — Start from DM (one row per subject)

```sas
data adsl;
  set sdtm.dm;
  keep studyid usubjid age sex arm armcd trt01p trt01a
       trtsdt trtedt saffl ittfl;
  /* Planned Treatment Period 01 = ARM from DM */
  trt01p = arm;
  /* Temporarily set actual = planned; refined later from EX/DS */
  trt01a = arm;
run;
```

---

## Step 1 — `SAFFL` (Safety Flag = received dose)

**Logic:** A subject is Safety (`SAFFL = "Y"`) if they received **at least one dose** of study drug. Source of truth is the **EX** domain (any record with `EXSTDTC` and `EXDOSE` > 0), optionally corroborated by **DS** (`DSDECOD = "DRUG RECEIVED"` / `"TREATMENT COMPLETED"`).

```sas
/* Flag subjects who received >=1 dose from EX */
proc sort data = sdtm.ex out = ex0;
  by usubjid exstdtc;
run;

data ex_dosed;
  set ex0;
  by usubjid;
  where not missing(exstdtc) and (missing(exdose) or exdose > 0);
  if first.usubjid then received = "Y";
  keep usubjid received;
run;

proc sort nodupkey data = ex_dosed;
  by usubjid;
run;

/* Merge onto ADSL */
proc sort data = adsl; by usubjid; run;

data adsl;
  merge adsl (in = a) ex_dosed (in = b);
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  if received = "Y" then saffl = "Y";
  else                  saffl = "N";
run;
```

---

## Step 2 — `ITTFL` (Intent-to-Treat Flag = randomized)

**Logic:** A subject is ITT (`ITTFL = "Y"`) if they were **randomized**. Best derived from **DS** (`DSDECOD = "RANDOMIZED"`), but can also be inferred from **DM.ARM** being non-missing and not `"NOT ASSIGNED"` / `"SCREEN FAILURE"`.

```sas
proc sort data = sdtm.ds out = ds_rand;
  by usubjid;
  where upcase(dsdecod) = "RANDOMIZED";
run;

data ds_rand(keep = usubjid randomized);
  set ds_rand;
  by usubjid;
  if first.usubjid then randomized = "Y";
run;

data adsl;
  merge adsl (in = a) ds_rand;
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  if      randomized = "Y"        then ittfl = "Y";
  else if not missing(arm) and
          upcase(strip(arm)) not in ("NOT ASSIGNED","SCREEN FAILURE")
                                   then ittfl = "Y";   /* fallback via DM.ARM */
  else                                ittfl = "N";
run;
```

---

## Step 3 — `TRT01P` (Planned Treatment, Period 01)

Already populated in Step 0:

```sas
trt01p = arm;          /* planned treatment = DM.ARM */
```

---

## Step 4 — `TRT01A` (Actual Treatment, Period 01)

**Logic:** Actual treatment reflects what the subject **actually took**. If actual = planned (the common case), `TRT01A = TRT01P`. When subjects discontinue or deviate, derive from **EX** (the treatment on the dosing records) or from **DS** discontinuation/`EPOCH`-level reassignment.

```sas
/* Pull the actual treatment from EX (EXTRT holds the treatment) */
proc sql;
  create table ex_trta as
  select distinct usubjid, extrt
  from sdtm.ex
  where not missing(extrt);
quit;

data adsl;
  merge adsl (in = a) ex_trta;
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  if not missing(extrt) then trt01a = extrt;   /* actual from EX  */
  /* else keep TRT01A = ARM set in Step 0     */
run;
```

> Note: If the study needs to reflect early discontinuation into an "actual" bucket, reconcile `TRT01A` against the DS disposition (`DSDECOD` in `("COMPLETED","DISCONTINUED")`).

---

## Step 5 — `TRTSDT` / `TRTEDT` (First / Last Dose Dates)

**Logic:** `TRTSDT` = earliest `EX.EXSTDTC`; `TRTEDT` = latest `EX.EXENDTC`, converted to true SAS date values via `input(.., yymmdd10.)`.

```sas
proc sort data = sdtm.ex out = ex_dates;
  by usubjid exstdtc;
run;

data firstdose lastdose;
  set ex_dates;
  by usubjid;
  /* first dose */
  if first.usubjid and not missing(exstdtc) then do;
    trtsdt = input(exstdtc, yymmdd10.);
    output firstdose;
  end;
  /* last dose — needs descending sort for clean first. capture */
run;

proc sort data = sdtm.ex out = ex_dates2;
  by usubjid descending exendtc;
run;

data lastdose;
  set ex_dates2;
  by usubjid;
  if first.usubjid and not missing(exendtc) then do;
    trtedt = input(exendtc, ymmdd10.);
    keep usubjid trtedt;
    output;
  end;
run;

data firstdose(keep = usubjid trtsdt);
  set firstdose;
run;

/* Aggregate alternative (robust): use PROC SQL min/max */
proc sql;
  create table trt_dates as
  select usubjid,
         min(input(exstdtc, yymmdd10.)) as trtsdt format = date9.,
         max(input(exendtc, yymmdd10.)) as trtedt format = date9.
  from sdtm.ex
  where not missing(exstdtc) or not missing(exendtc)
  group by usubjid;
quit;

proc sort data = adsl;      by usubjid; run;
proc sort data = trt_dates; by usubjid; run;

data adsl;
  merge adsl (in = a) trt_dates;
  by usubjid;
  if a;
  format trtsdt trtedt date9.;
run;
```

---

## Final — Keep/order analysis variables

```sas
proc sort data = adsl;
  by studyid usubjid;
run;

data adsl;
  retain studyid usubjid age sex arm armcd
         trt01p trt01a trtsdt trtedt saffl ittfl;
  set adsl;
  label
    trt01p = "Planned Treatment for Period 01"
    trt01a = "Actual Treatment for Period 01"
    trtsdt = "Date of First Exposure to Treatment"
    trtedt = "Date of Last Exposure to Treatment"
    saffl  = "Safety Population Flag"
    ittfl  = "Intent-to-Treat Population Flag";
run;
```

---

## Derivation Summary Table

| Variable | Source | Derivation |
|---|---|---|
| `SAFFL` | EX (+ DS corroboration) | `"Y"` if subject has ≥1 dose record (`EXSTDTC` present, `EXDOSE > 0`); else `"N"` |
| `ITTFL` | DS (fallback DM.ARM) | `"Y"` if `DSDECOD = "RANDOMIZED"` (or `ARM` not missing / not screen failure); else `"N"` |
| `TRT01P` | DM.ARM | Planned treatment, copied directly |
| `TRT01A` | EX.EXTRT (fallback DM.ARM) | Actual treatment taken; defaults to `TRT01P` |
| `TRTSDT` | EX.EXSTDTC | `min(EXSTDTC)` → date |
| `TRTEDT` | EX.EXENDTC | `max(EXENDTC)` → date |

